{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014yRaqcg6K5tH3XpSKJDDyy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the data:\n- This is a diagnostic paper about VLA safety evaluation\n- Target: CoRL 2026 / ICRA 2027\n- Core claims: Fake safety (strong), capability-safety anti-correlation (moderate), EE-only SDF limitation (strong), SDF produces real but extreme safety (strong)\n\nKey pending experiments:\n1. LoRA baseline (RUNNING, ETA ~09:30 UTC May 26) - determines SDF attribution strength\n\n\n2. Phase 2 λ=0 (RUNNING) - could strengthen the two-phase strategy narrative\n3. OpenVLA zero-shot eval (planned) - tests generalization\n4. spatial_bowl A1 training (RUNNING) - validates cross-scene robustness\n\nCurrent confirmed data shows Pi0.5 baseline at 74.7±1.5% TSR with 26.8±1.6% CAR, while Pi0.5+A1 SDF achieves 49-55% CAR but drops to 5-9% TSR with ~0.5m end-effector displacement and zero fake safety cases, whereas A1 on Pi0 reaches 91.5% CAR.\n\nThe A1 model on Pi0 shows 99.6% fake safety with 0% TSR, all three oracle variants underperform the baseline, and the baseline's safe episodes rely on geometric path safety rather than active avoidance. What really matters now is whether LoRA's baseline CAR matches the original ~27% to confirm SDF attribution, whether Phase 2 with λ=0 can achieve both TSR≥40% and CAR≥40% to validate the two-phase approach, and whether OpenVLA and spatial_bowl results demonstrate that fake safety or geometric path safety generalizes across model families and scenes.\n\nIn the best case, LoRA CAR stays near baseline so SDF gets full credit for the 25pp gain, Phase 2 succeeds with strong recovery, OpenVLA validates the pattern across a third model family, and spatial_bowl shows consistent cross-scene generalization—making this a diagnostic paper with a working solution. The median outcome has LoRA CAR moderate around 35-40% with SDF still contributing meaningfully, Phase 2 partially recovering TSR but losing CAR, OpenVLA showing ambiguous results, and spatial_bowl revealing weaker patterns—leaving us with a diagnostic paper that documents a useful method. In the worst case, LoRA CAR approaches SDF's level, Phase 2 fails to recover TSR, OpenVLA doesn't clearly show fake safety, and spatial_bowl shows no SDF effect, forcing a reframe toward pure evaluation methodology.\n\nNow I'm defining the specific metrics I need to track across these scenarios: LoRA-only CAR, the delta between SDF and LoRA performance, Phase 2 TSR recovery and CAR retention, OpenVLA's fake safety rate, spatial_bowl's SDF improvement, how many model families exhibit fake safety, and which scenes actually show SDF effects.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20524,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20524},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f3d5230-7cb5-4b16-ac4c-49672c3488ba","uuid":"348e40e5-6792-4381-9305-2b919180fcb3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014yRaqcg6K5tH3XpSKJDDyy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"SDF 归因强、Phase 2 成功、泛化充分 → diagnostic + solution paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"LoRA-only CAR ≈ baseline (~27-30%), SDF 获得 +20-25pp 全归因\"\n      - \"Phase 2 λ=0 达到 TSR≥40% + CAR≥40% → two-phase safety encoding 成立\"\n      - \"OpenVLA 在 object_pudding 展现 fake safety 或 geometric path safety → 第3 model family 验证 Claim 1\"\n      - \"spatial_bowl A1 训练产出 CAR 提升 ≥15pp over baseline → SDF 效果跨场景一致\"\n    number_ranges:\n      lora_only_CAR: [25, 32]\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_lora: [20, 28]\n      phase2_TSR: [40, 60]\n      phase2_CAR: [40, 55]\n      openvla_fake_safe_rate: [0.85, 1.0]\n      spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: [40, 55]\n      model_families_showing_fake_safety: [3, 3]\n      scenes_with_sdf_effect: [2, 2]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 全面升级。Claim 1-3 不变；Claim 4 从 \"real but extreme\"\n      升级为 \"two-phase training strategy that retains safety while recovering\n      task performance\"。论文定位从 diagnostic paper 升级为 diagnostic +\n      partial solution paper。R1 (generalizability) 用 3 model families +\n      2 scenes 应对；R3 (no solution) 被 Phase 2 直接化解；R5 (tradeoff\n      too extreme) 被 Phase 2 TSR 恢复数据反驳。acceptance 估算 65-75%。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"SDF 有效但非唯一驱动力、Phase 2 部分成功或失败、泛化有限 → 稳健的 diagnostic paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"LoRA-only CAR 中等 (~35-42%), SDF 仍提供 +10-18pp 有意义增量\"\n      - \"Phase 2 λ=0: TSR 恢复到 30-50% 但 CAR 回落至 30-35% → safety 需要持续 supervision（informative negative）\"\n      - \"OpenVLA eval 成功但 fake safety 信号弱于 Pi0（fake_safe_rate 60-85%），或 eval 部分失败需 debug\"\n      - \"spatial_bowl SDF CAR 提升 5-12pp → 效果存在但弱于 object_pudding\"\n    number_ranges:\n      lora_only_CAR: [33, 42]\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_lora: [10, 18]\n      phase2_TSR: [25, 50]\n      phase2_CAR: [28, 38]\n      openvla_fake_safe_rate: [0.55, 0.85]\n      spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: [30, 42]\n      model_families_showing_fake_safety: [2, 3]\n      scenes_with_sdf_effect: [1, 2]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 1 (fake safety) 仍为主贡献，证据链完整。Claim 4 需调整措辞：\n      \"SDF provides additive safety benefit beyond LoRA capacity, but LoRA\n      itself accounts for a non-trivial portion of improvement — geometric\n      supervision amplifies rather than solely drives collision avoidance.\"\n      Phase 2 结果作为 informative negative 写入：safety encoding 不持久，\n      需要持续 supervision。论文保持 diagnostic paper 定位，SDF 作为\n      验证工具（probe）而非 solution。R3 用 metric 贡献 + lambda 曲线作为\n      future work 应对。泛化数据薄但可通过 mechanistic argument 补偿。\n      acceptance 估算 50-60%。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"SDF 无增量、Phase 2 失败、泛化不足 → 需要 reframe 为纯 evaluation methodology paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"LoRA-only CAR ≈ SDF CAR (~48-55%), SDF 增量 ≈ 0 → 碰撞避免来自 LoRA capacity 而非 geometric supervision\"\n      - \"Phase 2 λ=0: TSR 不恢复 (<20%) → SDF 训练造成不可逆任务能力损伤\"\n      - \"OpenVLA eval 失败（推理 bug / 模型不兼容 SafeLIBERO）或 fake_safe_rate <50% 不支持 Claim 1 泛化\"\n      - \"spatial_bowl SDF 无 CAR 提升或训练 diverge → 效果局限于单场景\"\n    number_ranges:\n      lora_only_CAR: [45, 58]\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_lora: [-3, 5]\n      phase2_TSR: [0, 18]\n      phase2_CAR: [15, 55]\n      openvla_fake_safe_rate: [0.0, 0.55]\n      spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: [20, 32]\n      model_families_showing_fake_safety: [2, 2]\n      scenes_with_sdf_effect: [0, 1]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 4 (SDF method contribution) 被砍掉或降为 negative result appendix。\n      论文 reframe 为纯 evaluation methodology paper：(1) Claim 1 fake safety\n      metric 缺陷仍成立（2 model families 够用，mechanistic argument 补泛化）；\n      (2) displacement-filtered CAR 作为核心工具贡献；(3) LoRA capacity 而非\n      geometric supervision 驱动碰撞避免本身是有价值发现 — \"finetuning capacity\n      is sufficient, explicit geometric loss is neither necessary nor\n      sufficient\"；(4) Phase 2 不可逆损伤作为 cautionary finding。Block 5\n      改写为 \"what doesn't work and why\"。R3 (no solution) 压力增大，需\n      强化 metric 贡献的 standalone 价值 + 社区影响面。仍投 CoRL/ICRA，\n      但 framing 完全聚焦 evaluation methodology。acceptance 估算 40-50%。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20524,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20524},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f3d5230-7cb5-4b16-ac4c-49672c3488ba","uuid":"394a0738-e25b-4872-8d1a-87c50152a917"}
